From 45a6fbe63e6d488ade48f88690731f1e597c4a90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:51:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): [daveey] refuse a pinned skill the assignee
 cannot load; a stale pin never kills or retries a worker

A card created with skills=["x"] was accepted, every worker died at start with
'Error: Unknown skill(s): x', and the dispatcher retried it as a crash (escalating the
retry model) until the breaker gave up (hub card t_01a180e04c0b3a83).

- create time: kanban_create and 'hermes kanban create' check skills against the
  ASSIGNEE profile with the worker's own lookup (hermes_cli/kanban_skill_check.py);
  refusal code unknown_skill names close matches and creates nothing.
- start time (#119619): a dispatcher-owned kanban worker whose pins all miss starts
  with a prompt note naming them instead of exiting rc=1; interactive -s typo still fails.
- dispatcher: a worker that dies of 'Unknown skill(s)' is blocked kind=assignment on the
  first death, sticky, never retried.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_create_skill_validation.py (9; 6 red on base);
e2e worker contract KNOWN gate for #119619 removed (now passes).
